-- title:
--   Regular prolongation on the Igusa Gauss ring at q=2
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q = 2$, a non-zero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. The data are: a finite set $W$ of places of $\kappa$-modular function field `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,M' = \kappa(j, j_{M'})$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M'`$\kappa$ (rational affine geometric places at which the geometric $j$ takes a supersingular value); an inclusion $\iota$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the full level-$M'$ modular function field, into `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with values in `modularFunctionFieldC`$\kappa\,M'$, pinned coefficientwise (every Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is $R_0$-integral, with $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise reduction); a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$; families $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ and $O^{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'`, subject to: $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ is the Gauss ring of ratios $x/y$ of Laurent series with $A$-coefficients with $y$ of non-zero reduction; each $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ is the pullback of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M'` $\zeta\,\gamma$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ carrying $\infty$ to $\ell$; $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective; pullback along `levelAutBar q M'` $\zeta'\,\gamma$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, permutes the $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$; each $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ meets $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in $A$, is fixed by all these pullbacks, and admits an element $t$ with $t - a$ a unit for all $a \in A$; and each $R_0$-integral $f$ whose order is non-negative at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ where the $q$-expansion of $j$ has non-negative order and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation ring of $s$ has $\iota f \in O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, with $\iota f - a$ in the maximal ideal whenever the residue of $a \in A$ is the value of the $R_0$-residue of $f$ at $s$. Given moreover a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with values in `xHFunctionFieldC`$\kappa\,(q^2M')\,H$ whose ring of integers is $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, and the equivalence $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers} \iff \iota f \in O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, the conclusion is that there exists such a regular prolongation $R'$ with $R'.\mathrm{integers} = O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ for which, for every $R_0$-integral $f$, the element $\iota f$ is $R'$-integral and its $R'$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, coincides with the $R_0$-residue of $f$ read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case of the statement that the Gauss ring at the $\infty$-component of the Igusa covering carries a regular prolongation onto the concrete Igusa field inside $\kappa((q))$ whose residue map is coefficientwise $q$-expansion reduction, compatibly with the level-$M'$ constant reduction; for $q \le 3$ the Igusa covering of the $\infty$-branch has degree one. It feeds the count of Igusa nodes over the Gauss ring at $q = 2$, in the construction of the semistable covering of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$.
